   "text": "Prefer noeviction (or volatile-ttl) and size\nmemory generously, so failure is loud (errors,\nalerts), not silent. (volatile-ttl still evicts,\nsoonest expiry first: see diagram 5.)\nallkeys-lru silently turns the dedup store into a\ncache.",
   "originalText": "Prefer noeviction (or volatile-ttl) and size memory generously, so failure is loud (errors, alerts), not silent. (volatile-ttl still evicts, soonest expiry first: see diagram 5.)\nallkeys-lru silently turns the dedup store into a cache.",
   "fontSize": 20,
   "fontFamily": 5,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
